  "title": "Calorie estimates: bare counts of small discrete foods with no piece weight",
  "description": "About 100 lines (76 pipeline fixtures, 9 Paprika, 9 snapshots, plus 11 \"piece\" lines) count a food USDA doesn't weigh by the piece. \
Grouped: sausages (\"8 hot dogs\", \"3 hot dog sausages\" x2, \"4-6 smoked sausages\": frankfurter/kielbasa link weights from USDA Branded); candy (\"28 caramels\", \"24 gummy worms\", \"10 jujubees\", \"2/8 Fun Size Butterfinger\", \"2/4 candy canes\"); nuts and dried fruit (\"15 cashew nuts\", \"4/12 whole cashewnuts\", \"12/18 pecan halves\", \"12 walnut halves\", \"12 dried currants or raisins\"); olives and pickles (\"16 kalamata or other black olives\", \"6 to 7 pitted kalamata olives\", \"6 pepperoncini\", \"1 umeboshi\" x3, \"3 marinated artichoke hearts\" x3, \"3/4 canned artichokes\", \"2 jarred roasted red peppers\", \"1 roasted red pepper\"); spices counted (\"12 pods green cardamom\", \"24 whole cloves\": probably trace like bay leaves); citrus peel (\"3/4 strips lemon zest\", \"2 lemon twists\", \"1 orange peel\", \"1 piece lemon/orange peel\"); pasta and bread pieces (\"20 / 25-30 jumbo dried pasta shells\", \"6/4 whole wheat tortillas\", \"24 1/4-inch-thick baguette bread slices\" x3 and \"24 baguette slices or rye cocktail bread\" (a trailing \"slices\"; a baguette slice is not French bread's 64 g slice), \"12 to 16 1-inch thick rounds French bread\", \"16 sourdough toast fingers\" x3, \"2 piece sourdough or whole grain bread\" x3, \"2 piece toasted bread\"); \"12-15 thin slices pancetta\" (pancetta has no slice weight); \"2 layers sliced cheddar\" x3; \"12-15 green peas\", \"10-12 blackberries\", \"4 piece salmon fillets\", \"6-7 piece shrimp\", \"1 piece thick-cut bacon\", \"1 boneless rib eye steak\", \"1/0.25 Japanese leek\". \
Some lines aren't worth it (\"6 Pour the wine into the casserole…\" is an instruction captured as an ingredient; file that separately if it recurs). \
Take whole sub-groups with cited per-piece weights (USDA Branded labels give counts per serving for most packaged ones). \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit, all three corpora) and, once blocked-ingredient-burndown-from-prod lands, the prod report; make pipeline should produce only data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md and fixture-category diffs. \
Server-side only (ramekin-core nutrition), so no web or iOS change. \
Split out of the retired p3-nutrition-remaining-count-units (owner, 2026-10-24: whole groups per PR, never one ingredient).",
